{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614212057e3cd69fc91fc4e58","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see - the defaultAssignments function takes a model parameter that defaults to `{ provider: \"pi-lhc\", id: \"unconfigured\" }`. The issue is that \"unconfigured\" is classified as a placeholder.\n\nThe fix should be to change the default parameter to a non-placeholder value. Looking at the code comment \"Story 6 implements config loading; these defaults keep Story 5's production path on LHC inference by using PI's first available model when present\", it seems like the intent was to use PI's first available model, but that's done in defaultBuildSdkConfig.\n\nLet me check how defaultBuildSdkConfig works.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10094db-b1fb-4175-b007-bb5af83ee62f","uuid":"509f59b7-2d4a-42e2-a02c-9e41e0e6cd47"}
