{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614212140591e5a8b01fc4a3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The current TC-5.3 test only calls validateReachable and report, then asserts on the health state. To truly prove that \"affected lane derivations fail classified and queryable through health\", I need to:\n\n1. Create an LHC instance with assignments that have unreachable lanes\n2. Capture some content to trigger derivations\n3. Drain the scheduler to run derivations\n4. Inspect the thread to verify that:\n   - The affected lane derivations failed\n   - The failures are classified correctly\n   - The failures are queryable through health\n\nThis is a more complex test. Let me look at how the closed-loop test (TC-4.5) works to see the pattern for running derivations and inspecting results.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10094db-b1fb-4175-b007-bb5af83ee62f","uuid":"82c22bec-b084-47f2-b4f0-83469a365a64"}
