{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614212154decd50adeb114694","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is getting complex. The closed-loop test shows how to:\n1. Create a connector with custom assignments\n2. Capture content\n3. Drain the scheduler\n4. Inspect health for failed forms\n\nFor TC-5.3, I need to create a similar test that:\n1. Creates assignments with unreachable lanes (unknown provider/model)\n2. Creates an instance and captures content\n3. Verifies that validation reports unreachable lanes\n4. Runs derivations (or at least sets up the conditions)\n5. Verifies that the affected lane derivations would fail (or actually fail and are queryable through health)\n\nActually, looking at AC-5.3 more carefully: \"A validation failure leaves capture running. Derivations on the affected lanes fail, classified and queryable through health; the session is not broken.\"\n\nThe key is that:\n1. Capture continues after validation failure\n2. Derivations on affected lanes fail\n3. Those failures are classified and queryable through health\n\nThe current test already verifies #1 (capture continues) and that the validation report is in health. What it doesn't verify is #2 - that derivations actually fail.\n\nTo properly test this, I would need to:\n1. Create an instance with unreachable lane assignments\n2. Capture some content (which queues derivations)\n3. Let the scheduler run (drainSettled)\n4. Inspect health to verify the derivations failed with the correct classification\n\nThis is a significant addition to the test. Let me create a more comprehensive test.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10094db-b1fb-4175-b007-bb5af83ee62f","uuid":"5bf29f19-6317-4440-8876-62865899abb4"}
